---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Long Press is a daily tech brief written by Swami - eleven years of product at Vogue, GQ and Wired. Published every morning."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Masthead</span>
    <h1>About Long Press</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Press and hold. Everyone else tells you what happened; we stay on it a beat longer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <strong>Long Press</strong> publishes <a href="/daily">The Daily Five</a> every
      morning &mdash; five tech stories that mattered, each with an honest read on whether
      it actually changes anything. Alongside it run explainers and comparisons, and{' '}
      <a href="/known-issue">Known Issue</a>, a standing column on the things everyone is
      pretending aren&rsquo;t broken.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>
      Swami spent eleven years running product for Vogue, GQ, Wired, Condé Nast Traveller
      and Architectural Digest &mdash; twenty brand launches across five continents. Long
      Press is written from that side of the industry: someone who has shipped the things
      being reported on, rather than only covering them.
    </p>

    <h2>Cadence</h2>
    <p>
      Daily. The brief goes out every morning, India time. Where a story deserves more than
      a slot in the brief it gets its own page, and the brief links to it rather than
      repeating it.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Mistakes get fixed in place with a visible update line, not quietly. Reach the desk at
      <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com">builtbyswami@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <p>
      Long Press is published by <a href="https://www.builtbyswami.com">BuiltBySwami</a>,
      which also runs a <a href="https://www.builtbyswami.com/work-with-me">consulting
      practice</a> for publishers and media operators. The daily is free and always will be.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
